[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751207812","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104601#issuecomment-2751207812","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104601","id":2751207812,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j_BmE","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-25T13:08:09Z","updated_at":"2025-03-25T13:08:09Z","body":"Changing this isn't possible without breaking compatibility in pretty serious ways, and was rejected as a change in:\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102741\n\nWhere a different solution was chosen, so this is unlikely to change in 4.x","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751207812/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751264620","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104601#issuecomment-2751264620","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104601","id":2751264620,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j_Pds","user":{"login":"timoschwarzer","id":8849554,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDk1NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8849554?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer","html_url":"https://github.com/timoschwarzer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-25T13:28:04Z","updated_at":"2025-03-25T13:28:04Z","body":"@AThousandShips could you elaborate on where this would break? I did see that issue before but to me it looks like it was chosen not to change the type of the property because it was possible to fix *that issue* without. This issue however is impossible to workaround because there is no way to set the stretch transform on a Viewport other than setting `size_2d_override`, which is currently limited to integers.\n\nThe only way I can currently see this breaking any existing code if someone is currently setting `size_2d_override` to a Vector2 with fractional parts:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tvar some_size := Vector2(10.5, 10.5)\n\tviewport.size_2d_override = some_size\n```\n\nThis example would now yield in a different result because of the missing implicit conversion to Vector2i. I get that this is a breaking change and that it is eventually not desirable to merge until a new major version, but I imagine you have some bigger breakage in mind that I have overlooked when you talk about breaking compat in pretty serious ways. 👀 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751264620/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751284442","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104601#issuecomment-2751284442","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104601","id":2751284442,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j_UTa","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-25T13:34:45Z","updated_at":"2025-03-25T13:34:45Z","body":"This is not a bug to fix, it's at most a limitation to improve on, so breaking compatibility is a real concern. First of all this type is established *as* being integer valued, which informs use\n\nFurther C# uses properties exclusively so I'm unsure how this kind of breakgage is handled there\n\nFurther the actual viability of using non-integer scaling would need to be evaluated, just changing this type doesn't mean it will work properly, and I suspect there are other parts of the code that uses (or relies on) integer values, or at least don't support non-integers","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751284442/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751443670","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104601#issuecomment-2751443670","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104601","id":2751443670,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j_7LW","user":{"login":"timoschwarzer","id":8849554,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDk1NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8849554?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer","html_url":"https://github.com/timoschwarzer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-25T14:24:46Z","updated_at":"2025-03-25T14:27:10Z","body":"@AThousandShips Thank you! I didn't know C# doesn't use the compatibility getters/setters. The solution from the other PR is only a solution to that specific symptom in that issue though. The core issue still exists and has real usecases that aren't possible because of this.\n\n> First of all this type is established as being integer valued, which informs use\n\nAfter that logic this change should be no problem because `Viewport` already uses `Size2` and not `Size2i` for this property.  😅 It's only `SubViewport` that uses `Size2i`.\n\n> Further the actual viability of using non-integer scaling would need to be evaluated, just changing this type doesn't mean it will work properly, and I suspect there are other parts of the code that uses (or relies on) integer values, or at least don't support non-integers\n\nFrom what I can see, there are exactly two places that handle `size_2d_override`:\n\n- [Here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/6b5b84c0c50135e88691e035d3e00c68a2ae5aa4/scene/main/viewport.cpp#L1009-L1012) it is converted to the stretch transform. The resulting scale is already almost always non-integer.\n- And [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/6b5b84c0c50135e88691e035d3e00c68a2ae5aa4/scene/main/viewport.cpp#L1097-L1099) the size of the rect returned by `get_visible_rect` is set. This logic actually looks very flawed to me, because the visible rectangle is only the size of `size_2d_override` if 1. `size_2d_override_stretch` is enabled *and* 2. both components of `size_2d_override` are > 0.\n\nSo from what I gather, if set, `size_2d_override` actually does nothing but making `get_visible_rect` return a wrong value if `size_2d_override_stretch` is set to false. If `size_2d_override_stretch` is set to true, the stretch transform is derived from `size_2d_override` and the size of the rect returned by `get_visible_rect` is set to `size_2d_override`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751443670/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751451330","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104601#issuecomment-2751451330","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104601","id":2751451330,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j_9DC","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-25T14:27:09Z","updated_at":"2025-03-25T14:30:49Z","body":"(Please don't tag people who are already engaging in conversation, it's creating unnecessary noise for no reason)\n\nThe change to the property type in C# would risk introducing bugs as it changes the type, i.e. breaking compatibility, it uses the getters/setters internally but you can't use them in C#\n\n> After that logic this change should be no problem because `Viewport` already uses `Size2` and not `Size2i` for this property.\n\nThere's no such property","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751451330/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751472883","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104601#issuecomment-2751472883","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104601","id":2751472883,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kACTz","user":{"login":"timoschwarzer","id":8849554,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDk1NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8849554?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer","html_url":"https://github.com/timoschwarzer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-25T14:33:42Z","updated_at":"2025-03-25T14:33:42Z","body":"> There's no such property\n\nWrong word, my bad. I'm talking about `Size2 Viewport::size_2d_override`, which is a private member of `Viewport`. In the end `SubViewport` does nothing else than setting and getting that member.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751472883/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2768959719","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104601#issuecomment-2768959719","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104601","id":2768959719,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lCvjn","user":{"login":"KerekesDavid","id":9087461,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODc0NjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9087461?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid","html_url":"https://github.com/KerekesDavid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-01T10:49:31Z","updated_at":"2025-07-22T09:31:25Z","body":"I was about to work a bit on this as well (but got distracted for a few weeks, and it looks like the cavalry swooped in to help me out :D ). \n\nI came across the same limitation as @timoschwarzer here. I'm trying to use a high-resolution UI on top of a low resolution game in a subviewport, and the scaling of the pixels in the subviewport is all messed up depending on the user's screen resolution. \n\nBasically, because of the int size in subviewport, the bug from #102656 is still reproducible if you just put a full-scrreen subviewport inside your main viewport.\n\nIf we considered that a bug, I think we should consider this one a bug as well, and not outright reject the fix. \n\nI consider the previous fix a temporary stop-gap to make the worst of the bug go away, (hopefully for a good chunk of the developers), but the rest of the consequences will still need fixing.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2768959719/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2769033750","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104601#issuecomment-2769033750","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104601","id":2769033750,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lDBoW","user":{"login":"KerekesDavid","id":9087461,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODc0NjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9087461?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid","html_url":"https://github.com/KerekesDavid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-01T11:21:37Z","updated_at":"2025-04-01T11:31:57Z","body":"I wonder if we could use the proposed changes from https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/6221, deprecate size_2d_override and sidestep the compatibility breaking issue. How would you feel about that AThousandShips?\n\n(Also #72548 and similar issues seem to be related, and possibly could be fixed in one go. I wonder if @Sauermann or @stuartcarnie have any new insights, they seemed to be quite well spoken on the issue.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2769033750/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2769058289","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104601#issuecomment-2769058289","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104601","id":2769058289,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lDHnx","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscri